# Civil War Strategy: the Union navy against New Orleans (cws-whole-game, task 5.2; tools/screen/README.md, "Places
# and rules"). In March 1861 two ships are built and sail to New Orleans (the To menu takes a letter at once). In
# May, July and September they attack it: its forts are damaged twice, then it turns neutral. In November Attack is
# "-" (its key does nothing) and the ships land an army there (Invasion). Then END TURN by rules to the game's end,
# the Hall of Fame, Game Over, Quit.

# The waits of the computer's turns: a space each; a Retreat menu: the city it starts on; a main menu: END TURN;
# the End Turn and End Game menus: Yes. The Options at the end are answered by steps.
rule 1 key space
rule 3 key space
rule 4 key space
rule 5 key space
rule 6 key space
rule 7 key space
rule 8 key space
rule 9 key space
rule 10 key space
rule 12 key space
rule 13 key space
rule 14:M text e
rule 14:E text y
rule 14:R key enter

# The title menu: Start NEW Game; March 1861: Ships: Build twice, Sail to New Orleans; END TURN, Yes.
play until 14:C
digest
text s
play until 14:M
digest
text s
prompt
text b
prompt
text b
prompt
text s
prompt
digest
text n
prompt
text e
prompt
text y
# May, July and September: Ships: Attack; out; END TURN, Yes.
repeat 3
play until 14:M
digest
text s
prompt
text a
prompt
digest
key esc
prompt
text e
prompt
text y
end
# November: Ships: Attack is "-" (no key), Invasion.
play until 14:M
digest
text s
prompt
state
text a
prompt
text i
# The turns to the game's end by rules; the Options: Quit; the Hall of Fame: a name; Game Over; the title menu: Quit.
play until 14:O
state
text q
play until 11
state
text Grant
key enter
play until 14:C
digest
text q
repeat space
